      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2016 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Coronary embolization accounts for about 2% of ST elevation myocardial infarctions (STEMI). Thrombus aspiration may be particularly effective in these cases and may prevent the need for coronary stenting. Despite recent guidelines assigning a class III recommendation to routine thrombus aspiration, selective thrombus aspiration based on angiographic appearance may be effective."
      },
